181 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 182 0 R/Alt(Four panels. (a) A plan view of the held-out panel structure: a rectangular grid of gray beams about 0.36 m by 0.24 m with grid nodes as small dots, two dark squares marking components of 0.6 kg and 0.35 kg near the middle, a dashed purple vertical line marking a bolted lap joint between the second and third columns of nodes, hatched blue squares at the four corners marking the base blocks with their shakers, and open orange triangles at the same four corners marking the control accelerometers. (b) A side view drawn as a schematic: the panel as a gray bar with control triangles at its ends, carried at each end by a thin bracket spring beside a thick purple joint, standing on a hatched blue base block; each block rests on zigzag suspension springs on the ground, a dotted line between the blocks marks the fixture springs, and a blue arrow below each block marks the shaker force. (c) A plan view of the held-out frame: a grid of beams about 0.6 m by 0.36 m with a dashed lap joint line at 0.3 m, eight hatched blue squares marking the base blocks with shakers, twelve open orange triangles marking controls, and three dark squares marking components of 0.5, 0.4 and 0.3 kg. (d) A block diagram of the development structures: four blue arrows labeled shaker 1 to 4 enter a gray box saying that seven of them share eight modes at 72, 135, 210, 330, 520, 780, 1150 and 1650 Hz with 2 to 4 percent damping, and that in four each mode's frequency falls with its own recent amplitude; four dashed orange arrows labeled control 1 to 4 leave it. Below the box, a list of the development structures and how each softens, ending with the research model: four modes at 400, 700, 1100 and 1600 Hz, sampled at 20480 Hz, with its own target and an 8 percent drop set by the level.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[19]/Pg 774 0 R>>
endobj
