248 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 249 0 R/Alt(Two panels sharing a horizontal axis of pulse number from B (the buzz) to 15. Top: level in decibels relative to the full-level target. A small hatched gray bar at -20 dB marks the identification buzz. Open blue triangles mark three probe pulses at -40, -34 and -28.5 dB, filled orange circles mark ladder pulses (five at -12 dB, then -9, -6, -3 and -1.5 dB), and filled green squares mark three full-level pulses at 0 dB; the first and third full-level pulses are labeled. A dashed gray line marks the first ladder level at -12 dB. Bottom: the same pulses' over-test against their own level's target, between 0 and 1.8 dB, all below a dashed line at +3 dB marking the tolerance.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[5]/Pg 776 0 R>>
endobj
