278 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 279 0 R/Alt(A line plot of frequency drop in percent against test level from -40 to 0 dB. A solid gray band from 0.1 to 4 percent is labeled as measured on well-tightened bolted joints, and a hatched band from 4 to 10 percent as measured on loose or friction joints under shaker drive. Three development structures (first mode): moderate, a blue dashed line with open circles, rising from 0.24 percent at -40 dB to 3 percent from -18 dB on; severe, an orange solid line with open squares, rising from 0.68 percent at -40 dB to 6.1 percent at -24 dB and 8 percent from -18 dB on; non-saturating, a pink dash-dot line with open triangles, rising from 0.87 percent at -40 dB to 5 percent at -12 dB and 15 percent at full level. Two held-out panel variants (largest of nine modes): realistic joints, a green dotted line with open diamonds, rising to 1.7 percent at full level; low preload, a black dash-dot line with crosses, rising to 5.7 percent at full level. Vertical dotted lines mark the probes at -40 and -34 dB, the first ladder level at -12 dB and full level.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[15]/Pg 777 0 R>>
endobj
