344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 345 0 R/Alt(Two panels. (a) Log-log plot of the median error, in decibels, predicting the first -12 dB pulse's over-test, against the length of the identification buzz in seconds with the number of averages: 5 s (2), 10 s (4), 20 s (8), 41 s (16), 79 s (31), with a dotted line at 102 s (40) marking the identification used elsewhere. Held-out structures, frozen linear model (blue solid line, circles): 12.8, 0.61, 0.37, 0.36, 0.36 dB. Held-out structures, network with four low pulses (blue dashed line, squares): 13.9, 0.56, 0.09, 0.10, 0.19 dB. Unseen simulated structures, stress tier, frozen (orange solid line, triangles): 19.0, 4.7, 3.7, 3.1, 4.6 dB. The same with the network (orange dashed line, diamonds): 19.0, 5.2, 2.1, 1.9, 1.5 dB. (b) Worst point against the full-level target, in decibels, for each pulse of three runs on the held-out hardening panel. The network law (orange solid line, circles) climbs from -12 dB, crosses a dashed line at +3 dB at pulse 12 and swings between -1 and +5.2 dB through pulse 25. The followed family with its ceiling (blue dashed line, squares) rises to +1.7 dB and stays there. The frozen law (green dotted line, triangles) peaks at +4.5 dB at pulse 8, one full-level pulse, and ends near +2.3 dB.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[2]/Pg 780 0 R>>
endobj
