417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 418 0 R/Alt(Three panels, one per law, each showing the over-test in decibels of every full-level pulse, numbered 1 to 8, on the 32 percent spring at measurement noise 1e-3 for seeds 11 to 15. Each seed has its own color, line style and marker; filled markers are the first, third and last full-level pulses, open markers the others. A dashed line marks +3 dB. (a) The coupled corrector: seeds 12, 13 and 14 jump to 7.36, 5.97 and 8.87 dB at the second full-level pulse and 5.4 to 6.2 dB at the fourth, both open markers, while the judged first, third and last pulses sit near 2.0 to 2.4 dB; seeds 11 and 15 stay near 1.1 dB. (b) The hold rule: every pulse of every seed stays flat between 1.1 and 2.4 dB. (c) The followed family with its 12 percent ceiling: every seed falls smoothly from 1.6 to 0.9 dB.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[36]/Pg 783 0 R>>
endobj
